I am currently in a plan to move all my VMware vms to openshift virtualization, I have a application developed to ease the cluster builds, plan migrations, communicate the plan to respective gbgfs, to trigger migration jobs, track migration subtasks with mtv prehook and post hook jobs completed status updated to postgres. Prechecks would include the readiness of vms for migration i.e vcenters accessibility, vddk availability, vib installed, storage check for storage offloading and openshift csi readiness, vm disk space availability, vmtools installed etc. I am using react frontend, fastapi for api backend, postgres for database, to sync details about vm details from multiple VMware vcenters, service details, owners wo own it, applications running on it details etc details using airflow dag jobs and ingesting the data to database. I am using the data to plan vm migrations. And kafka to stream all the cluster builds requests, vm migration requests, configuration changes requests, new vcenters addition under scope of the application requests. Upstream I am using event driven ansible to trigger respective jobs and give feedback back to kafka topic , so job completed details get added to database on job execution is completed. As SRE, so far we have 3 main functionalities, i.e platform operations: daily platform level issues and identify the fix, if needed raise PR on gitops to fix the configs 2. lifecycle stream: argocd gitops releases when we get all the requirements inform of PR's, release tag is created from all the PR's and deployed when merged to sit and main branch. 3. migrations/hypercare stream: for daily migrations planned, SRE is responsible to identify if migrations are going as planned within scheduled CR window, if vm migrations are failing due to issues, SRE is responsible for identifying the issue, fix it and if it requires redhat assistance and it is going to take time. then take decision to rollback the vm to run back on vmware, hypercare is responsible for post issues on vm's once migrated, usually bsod, packet drops etc issues. all vm related resource expansion/addition requests goes through a different service which is out of scope.  i want use cases for migration. also please check for platformops, lifecycle streams are covered
